{
  "id": "ep171",
  "duration": 51.023,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.368,
      "text": "An explosion two billion light-years away physically rattled Earth's upper atmosphere.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA\u2019s Fermi, Swift Capture Revolutionary Gamma-Ray Burst (SVS14255 - GRB211211Apt).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - Scott Wiessinger, Aurore Simonnet, Jeanette Kazmierczak, Francis Reddy, Sophia Roberts, Aaron E. Lepsch",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA%E2%80%99s_Fermi,_Swift_Capture_Revolutionary_Gamma-Ray_Burst_(SVS14255_-_GRB211211Apt).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.368,
      "end": 14.588,
      "text": "On October 9, 2022, a massive star located within the constellation Sagitta violently collapsed directly into a black hole.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Sagitta (Annotated) (sagitta-ann).tiff",
        "credit": "E. Slawik/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/M. Zamani",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sagitta_(Annotated)_(sagitta-ann).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.367,
          "end": 9.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.933,
          "end": 14.6,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.588,
      "end": 20.483,
      "text": "The resulting gamma-ray burst was officially dubbed the BOAT, standing for Brightest Of All Time.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Fermi telescope illustration 04.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fermi_telescope_illustration_04.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.6,
          "end": 20.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.483,
      "end": 27.528,
      "text": "It completely smashed previous space records by being roughly seventy times brighter than any prior recorded burst.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Swift Observatory spacecraft model.png",
        "credit": "NASA E/PO, Sonoma State University/Aurore Simonnet",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swift_Observatory_spacecraft_model.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.467,
          "end": 24.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.167,
          "end": 27.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.528,
      "end": 35.198,
      "text": "The blinding flash was so intensely powerful that it temporarily saturated most gamma-ray space telescope detectors.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "James Webb Space Telescope (artist's impression) (jwst poster01).tiff",
        "credit": "ESA (C. Carreau)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Webb_Space_Telescope_(artist%27s_impression)_(jwst_poster01).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.533,
          "end": 30.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 35.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.198,
      "end": 44.123,
      "text": "Specialized lightning detectors across India and Germany picked up signals showing that the blast heavily ionized our upper atmosphere.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ISS053-E-222694 - View of Earth.jpg",
        "credit": "Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS053-E-222694_-_View_of_Earth.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.2,
          "end": 39.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 39.667,
          "end": 44.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.123,
      "end": 50.673,
      "text": "An explosion two billion light-years away shook Earth because its raw cosmic power was completely unmatched.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA\u2019s Fermi, Swift Capture Revolutionary Gamma-Ray Burst (SVS14255 - GRB211211Apt).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - Scott Wiessinger, Aurore Simonnet, Jeanette Kazmierczak, Francis Reddy, Sophia Roberts, Aaron E. Lepsch",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA%E2%80%99s_Fermi,_Swift_Capture_Revolutionary_Gamma-Ray_Burst_(SVS14255_-_GRB211211Apt).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.133,
          "end": 51.033,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
